            <ArticleTitle>A Spinal Circuit for Mechanically-Evoked Itch.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tins.2015.12.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0166-2236(15)00264-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A satisfactory neurobiological understanding of itch has proved difficult to reach. Bourane et al. have now uncovered a previously unrecognized spinal circuit for mechanically-induced itch and elucidated a mechanism that keeps it in check. Dysregulation of this circuit could contribute to chronic itch, suggesting a new strategy for itch relief.</AbstractText>
